{/snippet}

{#snippet bestPractices()}
  <Row>
    <LinkH2 href="/choicebox#best-practices" aria-label="best practices"
      >best practices</LinkH2
    >
    <div class="mt-4">
      <h3
        class="text-kui-light-gray-1000 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-1000 mb-2 text-[16px] leading-6 font-semibold tracking-[-0.16px]"
      >
        When to use
      </h3>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc">
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Use Choicebox when a choice benefits from a larger tap target plus a
          description or icon, like a framework picker, plan comparison, or
          deployment region with latency.
        </li>
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Single-select for mutually exclusive choices, multi-select for
          additive ones. Don’t mix the two within one group.
        </li>
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Cap at 4–6 tiles. Past that, switch to a <a
            href="/select"
            class="underline">Select</a
          >
          so the page doesn’t scroll for a single field. For plain text labels with
          no description, use <a href="/radio" class="underline">Radio</a>.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3
        class="text-kui-light-gray-1000 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-1000 mt-6 mb-2 text-[16px] leading-6 font-semibold tracking-[-0.16px]"
      >
        Behavior
      </h3>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc">
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          The whole tile is the click and focus target; tapping anywhere inside
          selects it. Don’t place nested buttons or links inside a tile that
          would steal the click.
        </li>
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Selected state shows a check or filled dot in the corner. The border
          highlight alone isn’t enough on low-contrast screens.
        </li>
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Disabled tiles need a <a href="/tooltip" class="underline">Tooltip</a>
          naming why ({@render roundedCode("Available on Pro")}). A faded tile
          with no reason reads as broken.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3
        class="text-kui-light-gray-1000 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-1000 mt-6 mb-2 text-[16px] leading-6 font-semibold tracking-[-0.16px]"
      >
        Content
      </h3>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc">
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Titles are parallel: one Title Case title plus one sentence-case
          description per tile, ending in a period.
        </li>
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Don’t restate the title in the description. The description adds the
          differentiator ({@render roundedCode("$20/mo · 100 GB bandwidth")}),
          not a synonym.
        </li>
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Icons are decorative when paired with a title; if the icon is the only
          label, give the tile an {@render roundedCode("aria-label")} naming the choice.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3
        class="text-kui-light-gray-1000 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-1000 mt-6 mb-2 text-[16px] leading-6 font-semibold tracking-[-0.16px]"
      >
        Accessibility
      </h3>
      <ul class="mt-2 list-disc">
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Tiles render as radios or checkboxes under the hood, so they are kept
          inside a {@render roundedCode("<fieldset>")} with a {@render roundedCode(
            "<legend>",
          )} so screen readers announce the group.
        </li>
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Arrow keys move within a single-select group, Space toggles in
          multi-select. Don’t override those keys with custom handlers.
        </li>
        <li
          class="[&_strong]:text-kui-light-gray-1000 text-kui-light-gray-900 dark:text-kui-dark-gray-900 mt-2 ml-8 py-0.5 leading-6 [&_strong]:font-normal"
        >
          Color is not the selection signal. Pair the highlight border with the
          corner check so colorblind users still see what’s active.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </Row>
{/snippet}

{#snippet prevAndNext()}
  <Row bottomLine={false}>
    <Pagination
      previous={{ title: "checkbox", href: "/checkbox" }}
      next={{ title: "collapse", href: "/collapse" }}
